# Recent births in the original continuous ensemble

Personal root derivation, fifth campaign, 2026-09-24. Conditional candidate,
not independently checked at creation. Preserve the original complete
formation instrument. This starts from the canonical N=4 state and is a
different problem from a normalized N=6 state at one specified birth.

## 1. Question and exact decomposition

Use the supplied compensated lambda=0 cube, fixed positive delta,K,kappa,
integer S, C=S(S+1), epsilon^2 C=delta/K, and the original resolved or coherent
marks L_i=sqrt(kappa) epsilon^-1 j_i. The system Hamiltonian is the physical
Hermitian H=delta epsilon^-4 h; the no-event generator in N is

    K_N=-i H_N-kappa Gamma_N/(2epsilon^2).

Start the full trace-one original GKLS ensemble from psi4=U4 Omega, with U4
the canonical Hermitian low embedding of the zero-field N=4 word. Let
v4(s)=exp(s K4) psi4. A first birth at time s with mark i, and no second birth
by time t, contributes the subnormalized pure density with ket

    x_i(s,t)=exp((t-s)K6) L_i v4(s).

Consequently the exact N=6 block is

    rho6(t)=sum_i integral_0^t |x_i(s,t)><x_i(s,t)| ds.       (1)

The other blocks are the N=4 no-first-birth ket and the N=8 second-birth
output. There is no return to N=6 after a second birth. The number blocks
are orthogonal and H preserves them. This is the full original law, without
introducing a finite marked amplitude or a time bin as a replacement law.

Fix t>0, independently of epsilon. We examine only the exact contribution
from first births whose age lies in [0,A epsilon^2], for a fixed A>0. The
rest of the original ensemble is retained when applying the final bound.

